    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10371" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπληρόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fill in turn</i> or <i>against,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ναῦς</span>
			<i>man</i> them <i>against</i> the enemy, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.69
			</span></i>, etc.:—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. φιλοτησίαν πρός τινα</span>
			<i>fill one's</i> cup in his honour, <i>pledge</i> him, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				2.115J.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>fill up by new members,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τάξεις ἐκ πολιτῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					2.2.26
				</span></i>
			; <i>replenish after exhaustion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				1.13.3
			</span></i>.</div>
